-- A column added by SCHEMA EVOLUTION, read from files written BEFORE it existed.
--
-- evolved_note was added after rows 1-800 were written, so those files do not contain the column at all. Iceberg's
-- reader materialises the projected schema rather than the file's, so the column comes back PRESENT WITH A NULL value
-- rather than absent. That is the opposite of a field that is not in the table schema at all, which is MISSING and is
-- omitted from the record entirely (see variant-predicate-shapes).
--
-- The two queries below are the decisive pair: IS MISSING must match nothing, IS NULL must match the old rows.
SELECT id, evolved_note FROM usersNoSnapshot WHERE id = 1;
